      "summaryMarkdown": "DOC-1: README and getting started show only the `tag = \"v1.0.0\"` form (diagnostics example included), point at the Releases page, state that `Cargo.lock` records the commit, that releases are Git tags only and that branch/`rev`/path dependencies are not used; the 0.1 promise and the path snippet are gone, and the README links `CHANGELOG.md` and `docs/releasing.md`. `doc-examples` passed with 135 tests (no new Rust blocks). DOC-2 (manual): `docs/releasing.md` covers every criterion bullet (release-PR flow with in-PR wording edits and the no-PR initial `v1.0.0`; 1.x policy incl. `Migration:` footer example, never `!`/`BREAKING CHANGE:`, `semver_check = false` and why, the three-point pre-merge check, `2.0.0` handling by rewording, and the policy end; `RELEASE_PLZ_TOKEN` owner/permissions/access list, why `GITHUB_TOKEN` is insufficient, silent expiry, missing-access failure and rotation; by-hand fallback through `gh release create`; immutable `v*` tags and fix-forward; push policy and `ci.yml` triggers; consumer pinning and bumping) with only toml/text/bash blocks, and is linked from `docs/20-contributing.md` and `docs/README.md`. Statements match `release-plz.toml` (git_only, publish=false, git_release_enable, release_commits, skipped chore scopes, `release = false` for doc-examples), `release-plz.yml` (release before release-pr, PAT at checkout) and `ci.yml` (pull_request + push to main); `cargo update -p rayx_reactive --offline` was dry-run verified. Nit (non-blocking): the fallback's `notes.md` is not said to be extracted from the new CHANGELOG section beyond the step comment. DOC-3: identical `## Releases` section in CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md before the AgentX block with all required items; the skill and its performance reference are commit-driven with the `Migration:` footer. The memory CHANGELOG rule is contradicted only as declared for promotion by `d-changelog-from-commits`.",
